{
  "_comment": "The Product Playground cast. Every company here is FICTIONAL - the names follow the convention Microsoft uses for sample data, and every domain is `.example`, which RFC 2606 reserves so it can never resolve. Nothing here describes a real organisation, and no payload generated from it should be read as intelligence about one. Real names were considered and rejected: fabricated buying signals attached to a real company are indistinguishable from real ones in a screenshot, and a demo that could be mistaken for a claim about somebody's business is a liability rather than an asset. Twelve accounts rather than two, because the design questions this exists to answer - does the row scan, does ranking beat grouping, does density hold - are unanswerable at two.",
